
=========
pure-midi
=========

.. default-domain:: pure
.. module:: midi
.. module:: midifile

Version @version@, |today|

Albert Graef <aggraef@gmail.com>

This is a MIDI interface for the Pure programming language (Pure 0.45 or later
is required). It includes the following modules:

* midi.pure: A PortMidi/PortTime wrapper which gives you portable access to
  realtime MIDI input and output. This uses PortMidi (by Roger B. Dannenberg
  et al) from the PortMedia project, see http://portmedia.sourceforge.net/.

* midifile.pure: Reading and writing standard MIDI files. This is based on
  David G. Slomin's light-weight midifile library, which comes bundled with
  the pure-midi sources.

For the public operations, read the source modules and bundled examples.
WINDOWS.md documents the supported Windows build, checked event layouts,
stream ownership, package verification and optional output testing.

Installation
------------

Sources are maintained at https://github.com/agraef/pure-lang.
On Windows, follow WINDOWS.md: use MSYS2 CLANG64 Clang/LLVM 22, Ninja,
portable Pure 0.68 and the audited PortMidi package. MSYS2 is the build
environment; installed executables and modules use native Windows runtimes.
The strict gate runs all mandatory Release/ASan no-hardware tests, recursive
PE verification, exact runtime/documentation installs and public make distcheck.
Package versions and hashes are intentionally checked; see THIRD_PARTY.md and
licenses/origins.tsv before changing dependencies.

Existing non-strict CMake and legacy Make builds remain available for upstream
platforms with Pure and PortMidi installed. Native POSIX behavior and Debian
source packaging have not been revalidated in the Windows audit. Historical
bundled PortMidi headers describe source origins, not modern Windows dependency
selection; strict builds consume the explicit CLANG64 headers/import library.

NOTE: You may also want to install the related pure-audio package. In
particular, pure-audio also provides realtime.pure, a little utility module
which gives Pure programs access to realtime scheduling.

